# Built by makezip.ps1 from the files beside it - what the page's "Download source"
# button serves. Derived from everything in this repo, so it does not belong in it.
AkaiS950Web.zip

# An 880 KB manifest of what the C# build makes of the disk library, for verify.js to
# diff the JavaScript against. Rebuild it with make-expected.ps1 when you need it.
expected.json

# Calibration takes: recordings of the sampler and of this page playing the same run,
# for benchcal.js to measure. Tens of megabytes each, and the numbers they settle are
# already written down in README.md.
*.wav
*.mp3
*.asd
*-report.txt

# The bench disk the self-test and the calibration run use. It is built by benchdisk.js
# from an original library image and carries that disk's audio with it, so it is kept out
# of a public repository:
#
#   node benchdisk.js build <an original .hfe> DSKA0000-bench.hfe
#   node benchdisk.js check DSKA0000-bench.hfe
#
# Any disk image works for the browser self-test; name it in the query string:
#   http://localhost:8080/selftest.html?disk=your-disk.hfe
DSKA0000-bench.hfe

node_modules/

# The LFO calibration disk, built from nothing by lfodisk.js - three generated tones and
# a 28-keygroup programme, both derived from lfoplan.js. Deterministic, so it is rebuilt
# rather than carried:
#
#   node tools/lfodisk.js build
#   node tools/lfodisk.js check tools/LFOCAL.img
tools/LFOCAL.img
tools/LFOCAL.hfe

# The filter envelope disks, built from nothing by envdisk.js - noise from a fixed seed and
# a programme whose every keygroup comes from the plan. Deterministic, so they are rebuilt
# rather than carried, the same as LFOCAL above:
#
#   node tools/envdisk.js build tools/ENVCAL
#   node tools/envdisk.js build tools/ENVCAL2 --plan envplan2.js
tools/ENVCAL.img
tools/ENVCAL.hfe
tools/ENVCAL2.img
tools/ENVCAL2.hfe
tools/ENVCAL3.img
tools/ENVCAL3.hfe
tools/ENVCAL4.img
tools/ENVCAL4.hfe
tools/ENVCAL5.img
tools/ENVCAL5.hfe
tools/ENVCAL6.img
tools/ENVCAL6.hfe
tools/ENVCAL7.img
tools/ENVCAL7.hfe

# What envcal.js --json writes, for envfit.js to turn into the envelope table.
#
# real4.json IS committed, beside this line: it is the whole of what a recording session
# with the hardware produced, the take itself being tens of megabytes and ignored above,
# and nobody can make it again without the machine. model4.json is the same analysis run
# over a render of the engine, so it is regenerable in two commands - and it would go stale
# silently the moment the engine's constants moved, which is exactly what it exists to
# measure against:
#
#   node tools/envrender.js envrendered4.wav tools/ENVCAL4.img --plan envplan4.js
#   node tools/envcal.js envrendered4.wav tools/ENVCAL4.img --plan envplan4.js --json model4.json
tools/model4.json

# Cloudflare Pages serves landing/ and nothing else - one page whose only job is to link
# to the GitHub Pages site, which is where the app actually lives. Deliberately not a copy
# of the app: a second copy would need deploying on every change and would silently fall
# behind the moment one was missed.
#
#   wrangler pages deploy landing --project-name akais950web --branch main
#
# landing/ is source and is committed. .wrangler is wrangler's own cache of which account
# it is talking to, and is not.
.wrangler/
